    "opening": "A small-business valuation is a supported estimate of what a defined business interest is worth at a stated date. State whether the figure concerns operating assets, enterprise value or the owners’ equity. Compare methods on compatible earnings, cash and debt assumptions, and report a range with evidence instead of treating one multiple as a market price.",
    "answerHtml": "<p>A small-business valuation is a supported estimate of what a defined business interest is worth at a stated date. State whether the figure concerns operating assets, enterprise value or the owners’ equity. Compare methods on compatible earnings, cash and debt assumptions, and report a range with evidence instead of treating one multiple as a market price.</p>",
