    "id": "N070",
    "slug": "gross-profit-gross-margin",
    "title": "Gross Profit and Gross Margin: Formula and Reconciliation",
    "seoTitle": "Gross Profit and Gross Margin: Worked Example",
    "description": "Calculate gross profit and gross margin from net revenue and matched COGS. Reconcile a checked inventory case and separate fees, contribution and net income.",
    "metaDescription": "Calculate gross profit and gross margin from net revenue and matched COGS. Reconcile a checked inventory case and separate fees, contribution and net income.",
    "primaryKeyword": "gross profit and gross margin",
    "scopeBoundary": "Owns the net-revenue-to-COGS gross-profit bridge, not the margin-versus-markup interactive calculator, net-revenue deductions or final net-income calculation.",
    "opening": "Gross profit is net revenue minus the cost of goods sold or cost of sales on the stated reporting basis. Gross margin is that gross profit divided by net revenue. Reconcile both inputs for the same period before interpreting the percentage, and keep selling costs, financing, tax and customer cash separate from the gross-profit subtotal.",
    "answerHtml": "<p>Gross profit is net revenue minus the cost of goods sold or cost of sales on the stated reporting basis. Gross margin is that gross profit divided by net revenue. Reconcile both inputs for the same period before interpreting the percentage, and keep selling costs, financing, tax and customer cash separate from the gross-profit subtotal.</p>",
    "answerTitle": "Quick answer",
